{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105368","id":2456326226,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6SaJBS","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105368","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105368.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105368.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105368","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105368/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105368/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105368/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/294303eac960eee90694cd663b8f8a55a7a2ffaf","number":105368,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add inspector support for typed property hint formats","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Currently, the editor supports two methods of typing dictionaries and arrays, with the `PROPERTY_HINT_ARRAY_TYPE` hint (and the dictionary alternative), and the `PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING`. These type hints have different formats, and so need to be handled separately. That being said, the inspector currently does not accept the `PROPERTY_HINT_ARRAY_TYPE` and `PROPERTY_HINT_DICTIONARY_TYPE` formats, and so does not understand the associated type hints. This leads to nodes such as the GraphEdit's type_names property not having the proper inspector editor when creating a key/value pair (instead being the general object one).\r\n\r\nFor reference; `PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING` is of the format `\"%s:%s/%s\" % [Variant::Type type, PropertyHint hint, String hint_string]`, while `PROPERTY_HINT_ARRAY_TYPE` is the human-readable class name like `\"Texture2D\"`.\r\n\r\n| Before; the add key and value are not typed: | After |\r\n| - | - |\r\n| <img width=\"335\" alt=\"Before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad1b1a7c-71cf-4650-a3cf-217bd0bc1c32\" /> | <img width=\"334\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-04-14 at 10 21 24 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/462dd742-092f-4a32-9d09-804dbf658134\" /> |\r\n\r\n\r\nThis PR allows the inspector to receive this format, as well as adding the relevant documentation to the PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING and PROPERTY_HINT_ARRAY_TYPE constants.\r\n\r\nSee also: #100926 \r\nA bit outdated but also: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/78656/files#r1736538595\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJ